{#
	Widgets for the engine's own form types (XIV-11).

	Registered in the application's twig configuration alongside Bootstrap's own
	theme, and kept here rather than there because how a core field type looks is
	core's business — a module or an application should not have to know that a
	price is drawn with something in front of it.
#}

{#
	The amount, with the installation's currency in front (XIV-11, §8.6).

	`currency` comes from MoneyAmountType::buildView and is null until somebody
	has chosen one on the profile page. A plain input then, rather than an empty
	box in front of the number: an input group with nothing in it reads as a
	rendering fault.
#}
{% block xivi_money_amount_widget %}
	{% if currency is null %}
		{{- block('form_widget_simple') -}}
	{% else %}
		<div class="input-group">
			<span class="input-group-text">{{ currency }}</span>
			{{- block('form_widget_simple') -}}
		</div>
	{% endif %}
{% endblock %}
